-- Extra drops of the Metin stones and the bosses, the world's choice
-- (Jeremus-Sama, 1 October: "Metin and boss drop settings ... quantity and
-- quality depends on metin level and boss difficulty"). Two event flags are
-- the percent a person's kill rolls at: m2_extra_ds_drop for the Dragon Stone
-- Alchemy's material (a Metin stone's shards, a boss's Cor Draconis) and
-- m2_extra_coupon_drop for a Kupon SM by the victim's level and rank. The
-- migrator writes both from .env (M2_EXTRA_DS_DROP, M2_EXTRA_COUPON_DROP; 0,
-- the default, is the world as it was) and the classic panel sets them live.
--
-- What drops and for whom is m2_difficulty.lua's (m2_world_drops), a plain
-- Lua file the quest libraries load, where the rules are told and tested
-- (tests/quest_world_settings_test.sh). The kill handler asks the two flags
-- first: with both at 0 a kill costs two flag lookups and nothing else, and
-- a bot's kill goes no further either (pc.is_playerbot inside).
quest world_drops begin
	state start begin
		when kill with game.get_event_flag("m2_extra_ds_drop") > 0 or game.get_event_flag("m2_extra_coupon_drop") > 0 begin
			m2_world_drops_kill()
		end
	end
end
